<title>FRANCE: Bomb blasts bank in northern Corsica.</title>
<headline>Bomb blasts bank in northern Corsica.</headline>
<dateline>AJACCIO, Corsica 1997-01-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>A bomb exploded overnight outside a bank in Montesoro, northern Corsica, police said on Saturday.</p>
<p>The bomb, consisting of about 100 grams (a quarter pound) of dynamite, caused minor damage to the branch of the Credit Agricole Bank but there were no casualties, police said.</p>
<p>No one immediately claimed responsibility for the blast but Corsican separatist guerrillas seeking greater autonomy from mainland France stage regular bombing attacks on the island.</p>
</text>
